.TH WLIST-UPDATE 1 "17 November 2026" "version 0.1.1"
.SH NAME
wlist-update \- update item and note details.
.SH SYNOPSIS
wlist update [path/to/database]
[--item-id <item id> | -i <item id>]
[--note-id <note id> | -n <note id>] 
[--name <item>][--quantity <amount> | -a <amount>]
[--priority <priority level> | -p <priority level>]
[--url <url> | -u <url>]
[--notes <Notes>...][--note <note>]
[--remove-note | -r][--append-note | -a]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Update items and notes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -i <item id>, --item <item id>
The item to update.
.TP
.B -n <note id>, --note-id <note id>
The note to handle.
.TP
.B --name <item>
The name of the item.
.TP
.B -q <amount>, --quantity <amount>
The quantity of the specified item.
.TP
.B -p <priority level>, --priority <priority level>
How much you want the item.
.PP
The value can be one of the following:
.RS
.IP
low
.IP
medium
.IP
high
.IP
highest
.RE
.TP
.B -u <url>, --url <url>
The URL for the item.
.TP
.B --notes <Notes>...
A list of notes regarding the item.
.PP
When providing a note, 
make sure to put the note in quotes,
unless the note is only one word.
.PP
If quotes are not used, 
each item is considered its own note.
.TP
.B --note <note content>
specify note content.
.PP
Because things can get confusing otherwise,
This can only be used when updating notes themselves.
.PP
If you want to add notes that don't exist to items,
use
.B --notes
.TP
.B -r, --remove-note
Tell program to remove a note 
with the specified id from the specified item.
.TP
.B -a, --append-note
Tell the program to append a note 
with the specified id to the specified item.
.SH AUTHOR
Bryce Campbell (tonyhawk2100@gmail.com)
.SH EXAMPLES
Add notes to item:
.RS
.IP
wlist update -i FF04C3DC-F0FE-472E-8737-0F4034C049F0 --notes hello world 
.RE
.PP
Add exist note to item:
.RS
.IP
wlist update -i FF04C3DC-F0FE-472E-8737-0F4034C049F0 -n 1 -a
.RE
.PP
Update note:
.RS
.IP
wlist update -n 1 --note "Hello, World!"
.RE
.PP
Add item with priority level:
.RS
.IP
wlist -n "Mario Kart" -p high
.RE
.PP
Add item with URL:
.RS
.IP
wlist add -name "Mario Kart" -u https://example.com/mario-kart
.RE
.PP
Add item a quantity of more than 1:
.RS
wlist add -n "Mario Kart" -q 2
.RE